    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d47">

                <pb facs="0166" n="60" sameAs="frus:frus1906p1/pg60"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Department of State to the
                            Belgian Legation.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Memorandum.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State.</hi><lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1906-03-19"><hi rendition="#italic">March 19,
                        1906</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>The Department of State has the honor to acknowledge receipt of the memorandum of
                    the Belgian minister dated March 8, 1906, concerning the claim of the Belgian
                    firm El Oriente, and has also received the minister’s note relating to the same
                    subject, of the same date, and the three inclosures transmitted thereby.</p>
                <p>The Department of State begs to say that a careful reexamination has been made of
                    all the documentary evidence, including the exhibits inclosed with the Belgian
                    minister’s notes, and regrets to inform the minister that it has been unable to
                    perceive any reason to change the views expressed in its memorandum dated
                    February 15, 1906; and that this Government must, therefore, decline to assume
                    any responsibility in the premises.</p>
            </div>
